Well, except that neither is either, since the la.djan and la.gleki both ap=
pear to be human males.  However, {djan} is a cmevla (the {la} and the paus=
es are not parts of the name but parts the apparatus for using it to refer =
to someone). gleki} is, as noted, a gismu. Like any Lojban word (well, almo=
st any), it can be used to name something/one by enclosing it in pauses and=
 slapping a {la} in front.  To that extent it is a cmene (and also the fact=
 that someone actually uses it in this way).  In short, cmevla are inherent=
ly cmene s re strings of cmevla; everything else is a cmene only insofar as=
 occurs after {la} (etc.) and enclosed in pauses. (Should {cmene} perhaps b=
e reserved for {la. ... .} expressions or would that introduce a new confus=
ion where people, asked for their names, gave things that astarted with {la=
} and ended witha pause?



